---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../../../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import MadeByKaj from '../../../components/MadeByKaj.astro';
import LiveCodePlayground from '../../../components/live/LiveCodePlayground.astro';
import CodeBlockWithCopy from '../../../components/live/CodeBlockWithCopy.astro';
import { applySkykitLiveVersions } from '../../../config/skykit-live';
import chapterButtonsHtmlSource from '../../../live-examples/skykit/journey-buttons/index.html?raw';

const basePath = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const chapterButtonsHtml = applySkykitLiveVersions(chapterButtonsHtmlSource);
const chaptersCode = `const SUN_PC = { x: 0, y: 0, z: 0 };
const ICRS_NORTH = { x: 0, y: 0, z: 1 };
const PLEIADES_PC = { x: 67.379, y: 103.162, z: 55.161 };
const ORION_NEBULA_PC = { x: 44.371, y: 409.774, z: -38.889 };
const ORION_TILTED_ORBIT_NORMAL = { x: -0.35, y: 0.45, z: 0.82 };

const chapters = {
  solarOrbit: {
    label: '1 pc Sun orbit',
    center: SUN_PC,
    radiusPc: 1,
    angularSpeedRadPerSec: 0.22,
    normal: ICRS_NORTH,
    durationSecs: 4,
  },
  pleiadesOrbit: {
    label: 'Wide Pleiades orbit',
    center: PLEIADES_PC,
    radiusPc: 32,
    angularSpeedRadPerSec: 0.08,
    normal: ICRS_NORTH,
    durationSecs: 8,
  },
  orionNebulaOrbit: {
    label: 'Tilted Orion Nebula orbit',
    center: ORION_NEBULA_PC,
    radiusPc: 120,
    angularSpeedRadPerSec: 0.045,
    normal: ORION_TILTED_ORBIT_NORMAL,
    durationSecs: 10,
  },
};`;
const buttonCode = `document.querySelector('#sun-orbit').addEventListener('click', () => {
  goTo('solarOrbit');
});

document.querySelector('#pleiades-orbit').addEventListener('click', () => {
  goTo('pleiadesOrbit');
});

document.querySelector('#orion-orbit').addEventListener('click', () => {
  goTo('orionNebulaOrbit');
});`;
---

<Layout
	title="Automate SkyKit chapters | Found in Space"
	description="Create named SkyKit chapter functions, including orbit scenes, then wire buttons to the chapter dispatcher."
>
	<SiteHeader section="Learn & build" />

	<main class="page page--lesson">
		<header class="lesson-hero">
			<nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
				<a href={`${basePath}learn-build/`}>Learn &amp; Build</a>
				<span class="breadcrumb__sep" aria-hidden="true">›</span>
				<a href={`${basePath}learn-build/skykit/`}>SkyKit</a>
				<span class="breadcrumb__sep" aria-hidden="true">›</span>
				<span>Chapter automation</span>
				</nav>
				<p class="eyebrow">Lesson 3</p>
				<h1>Automate chapters</h1>
				<p class="lede">
					Turn camera movement into destination buttons: enter a solar orbit from the current
					view, insert around the Pleiades, then arrive on a tilted orbit around the Orion
					Nebula.
				</p>
		</header>

		<article class="lesson-body prose">
			<section>
				<h2>Learning goal</h2>
				<p>
					Lesson 2 called individual transitions directly. This lesson gives those ideas
					chapter semantics: named functions, orbit cameras, and direct navigation actions.
				</p>
					<p>
						The buttons only choose chapters. Each chapter owns its target, orbit camera, duration, and orbital plane.
					</p>
			</section>
		</article>

			<LiveCodePlayground
				id="skykit-chapter-automation"
				title="Chapters from the Sun to Orion"
				description="Use the buttons to enter a 1 pc solar orbit, fly to the Pleiades, or insert around the Orion Nebula on a tilted plane."
			initialCode={chapterButtonsHtml}
			mode="html"
			height="36rem"
		/>

		<article class="lesson-body prose">
			<section class="callout panel">
				<p class="panel__eyebrow">Things to try</p>
				<ul>
					<li>Change the Pleiades or Orion <code>radiusPc</code> values to tighten or widen the inserts.</li>
					<li>Change <code>ORION_TILTED_ORBIT_NORMAL</code> to see the arrival plane change.</li>
					<li>Add another chapter key with its own target and orbit settings.</li>
					<li>Adjust each chapter's <code>durationSecs</code>.</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

				<section>
					<h2>What changed in the code</h2>
					<p>
						The chapter table is ordinary app code. When a button calls <code>goTo()</code>, the selected chapter invokes navigation actions and starts an orbit after arrival.
					</p>
				<CodeBlockWithCopy code={chaptersCode} label="Chapter table" language="js" />
				<CodeBlockWithCopy code={buttonCode} label="Button wiring" language="js" />
			</section>

			<section class="source-panel panel">
				<p class="panel__eyebrow">Next step</p>
				<h2>Move the same pattern into a local app.</h2>
				<p>
					The quickstart embed is useful for learning, but the same browser handle exists
					when you install SkyKit in Vite and import it from npm.
				</p>
				<ul>
					<li><a href={`${basePath}learn-build/skykit/add-an-object/`}>Next: use SkyKit in a local app</a></li>
				</ul>
			</section>
		</article>

		<MadeByKaj />
	</main>
</Layout>
